# Airsyntax

A high-performance, bilingual (English/Chinese) desktop relay and bridging utility designed for seamless real-time text transmission and synchronization between desktop environments and multiple target iPhones. Airsyntax utilizes a robust local WebSocket architecture coupled with secure dynamic tunneling to establish instantaneous, zero-configuration remote connectivity without external runtime dependencies.

---

## Architecture & System Overview

Airsyntax is engineered as a self-contained desktop application that integrates an asynchronous ASGI server lifecycle directly alongside a native operating system window manager.

* **Core Backend Framework**: Built on Python using **FastAPI** for high-throughput asynchronous request routing and native **WebSockets** for real-time bi-directional message dispatching.
* **Embedded Desktop Runtime**: Utilizes **PyWebView** to render a clean, frameless, and flicker-free native window container, eliminating traditional browser chrome and system command prompt dependencies.
* **Dynamic Tunneling Engine**: Integrates automated tunnel orchestration to securely expose local socket instances to remote mobile clients instantly upon application startup.
* **Multi-Device Client Scaling**: Supports concurrent multi-client connections simultaneously, allowing an unlimited number of connected iPhones to receive broadcast streams or push data back to the host system in real time.

---

## Key Features

* **Bilingual Support**: Available in dedicated English (`server_en`) and Chinese (`server_zh`) interface implementations tailored for localized workflow integration.
* **Instant QR Provisioning**: Automatically generates and renders dynamic session QR codes upon tunnel activation, allowing immediate scanning and connection from iPhones.
* **Bi-Directional Real-Time Relay**:
* *Desktop-to-iPhone*: Broadcast text payloads, notes, or formatted strings instantly to all connected iPhones.
* *iPhone-to-Desktop*: Push captured or edited text directly back from mobile clients to the host computer interface with automated clipboard synchronization.


* **Zero System Footprint**: Operates entirely as a portable standalone executable requiring no manual network configuration or background service installation on target machines.

---

## Technical Specifications

| Component | Technology / Protocol |

| **Server Runtime** ⸺ Python, Uvicorn, FastAPI |
| **Desktop Interface** ⸺ PyWebView (Native Web Container) |
| **Communication Protocol** ⸺ WebSockets (`/ws`, `/admin-ws`), HTTP JSON API |
| **Tunneling Layer** ⸺ Secure Dynamic Tunnel Routing |
| **Client Target** ⸺ iOS / iPhone Safari Web Client |

---

## Usage Guide

1. Launch the compiled executable on the host machine.
2. Wait for the initialization sequence to complete and the dynamic connection tunnel to establish.
3. Scan the generated QR code using the camera or a QR reader on your **iPhone** to open the secure mobile relay interface.
4. Type or paste text into the desktop control panel and click **Push to All iPhones** (or equivalent localized button) to broadcast instantly.
5. Incoming payloads pushed from any connected **iPhone** will automatically populate the desktop interface with options for immediate clipboard copying.
